menu "Lamp"

config LAMP_ENCODER_STEPS
    int "Encoder detents from off to full brightness"
    range 2 100
    default 30
    help
        30 is one full turn of the EC11. The steps rise in equal ratios from
        LAMP_MIN_BRIGHTNESS_PERMILLE to 100 %, so each one looks about as big.

config LAMP_MIN_BRIGHTNESS_PERMILLE
    int "Brightness of the first encoder step (permille of full)"
    range 1 1000
    default 20
    help
        SK6812 channels are 8 bit, so much lower makes dim colours drop out.

config LAMP_DEFAULT_BUDGET_MA
    int "Default LED current budget (mA)"
    range 50 2000
    default 1600
    help
        The highest budget allowed, so the full chain can reach full
        brightness (70 LEDs at full white take about 1.2 A). A laptop USB port
        may not supply that; lower it with 'budget', e.g. 400. Capped 200 mA
        below LAMP_OVERCURRENT_MA.

config LAMP_OVERCURRENT_MA
    int "Measured LED current that latches LED power off (mA)"
    range 300 2200
    default 1800
    help
        Just under U402's 2.04 A limit. The budget is capped 200 mA below.

endmenu
